{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And you shall eat, and shall not be ashamed</b> — the opposite of <i>the farmers are ashamed</i> (הובישו אכרים). And they are two roots; the meaning is one. And like it: <i>take counsel, and counsel</i> (יעץ ועוצו עצה)."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra argues that הובישו (were ashamed, v. 26) and הובישו אכרים (the farmers are ashamed, v. 11) derive from two different roots, yet share the same meaning; he cites Isaiah 8:10 as a parallel case of two formally distinct roots bearing identical sense."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:38.267412477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}